.TH TUI_MDVIEW_INIT 3 2026-11-11 "libtuikit 1.2" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_mdview_init, tui_mdview_free, tui_mdview_set_text,
tui_mdview_set_plain, tui_mdview_lines, tui_mdview_top,
tui_mdview_scroll, tui_mdview_scroll_to, tui_mdview_scroll_end,
tui_mdview_handle, tui_mdview_render, tui_md_render,
tui_md_render_marked, tui_md_strip_marks \- Markdown shown readably
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/mdview.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_mdview_init(tui_mdview *" mv );
.BI "void tui_mdview_free(tui_mdview *" mv );
.BI "int  tui_mdview_set_text(tui_mdview *" mv ", const char *" md );
.BI "void tui_mdview_set_plain(tui_mdview *" mv ", int " plain );
.BI "int  tui_mdview_lines(const tui_mdview *" mv );
.BI "int  tui_mdview_top(const tui_mdview *" mv );
.BI "void tui_mdview_scroll(tui_mdview *" mv ", int " delta );
.BI "void tui_mdview_scroll_to(tui_mdview *" mv ", int " line );
.BI "void tui_mdview_scroll_end(tui_mdview *" mv );
.BI "int  tui_mdview_handle(tui_mdview *" mv ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_mdview_render(tui_mdview *" mv ", tui_canvas " c ", tui_style " st );
.PP
.BI "int  tui_md_render(const char *" md ", int " width ", int " ansi ", tui_buf *" out );
.BI "int  tui_md_render_marked(const char *" md ", int " width ", tui_buf *" out );
.BI "int  tui_md_strip_marks(const char *" marked ", tui_buf *" out );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Markdown view shows Markdown \(em the description and the comments of a
ticket, any other Markdown \(em the readable way, the same in every program:
never raw, and with no renderer of the program's own.
It keeps its own copy of the text, scrolls, and follows the width it is
drawn at.
.PP
Supported: headings
.RB ( # " to " ######;
the first two are underlined with
.B =
and
.BR \- ),
bold
.RB ( **x " and " __x__ ),
italic
.RB ( *x " and " _x_ ;
an underscore inside a word stays),
code spans and fenced blocks
.RB ( \(ga\(ga\(ga " and " ~~~ ),
bullet
.RB ( \- ", " * ", " + )
and numbered lists with nesting by indent, block quotes, tables
.RB ( | ),
links
.RB ( [text](url) ,
shown as
.RB \(lq "text (url)" \(rq),
and the backslash escapes.
Control characters in the source, a tab among them, are shown as spaces.
.SS Reflow
Text in a ticket is often broken at a fixed width by the author's tool.
The lines of one paragraph are joined with a space and wrapped again to the
real width: a line break means a new paragraph only after an empty line.
A list item is one line (an indented line after it continues it), the lines
of a code block are kept, and the lines of a block quote are one paragraph
until an empty quote line.
A word wider than a line is split at the column.
A table is fitted to the width by shortening its widest column with
.RB \(lq ... \(rq.
.SS The summary
The first paragraph of the text is the summary: it is set apart by a blank
line and drawn in bold.
A text that starts with another block has none.
.SS The view
.BR tui_mdview_set_text ()
replaces the text and scrolls to the top.
.BR tui_mdview_render ()
renders the Markdown to the canvas width if the text or the width changed,
clears the canvas with
.IR st ,
and draws the visible lines on the background of
.IR st :
headings in the role
.B accent
(bold), code in the colour of the role
.BR hint ,
bold and the summary in bold, italic in italic.
A span that wraps carries on in the next line.
When the text is longer than the canvas, the last column is a scroll bar
(roles
.B scrollbar.track
and
.BR scrollbar.thumb ),
and the text is one column narrower only while the bar is shown.
.PP
.BR tui_mdview_set_plain ()
with 1 is the plain fallback: every cell is drawn in
.IR st ,
no colour and no attribute, the lines the same.
.PP
.BR tui_mdview_handle ()
applies Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn (one view less one line), Home and End, and
the shared letters
.RB ( j ", " k ", " ctrl\-f ", " ctrl\-b ", " g ", " G ),
and returns 1 for them.
Esc,
.B q
and Backspace go back one level; they are the program's, and F8 (freeze) is
the program's too, as for the other views.
.BR tui_mdview_lines ()
is the number of lines at the last render width.
.SS As text
.BR tui_md_render ()
appends the rendering to
.I out
for a program that prints (an export, a pipe): wrapped at
.I width
columns (at least 20), as plain text with
.I ansi
0, with SGR sequences (bold, italic, cyan code; each line resets its own)
with 1.
.BR tui_md_render_marked ()
keeps zero-width marker bytes
.RB ( TUI_MD_BOLD ", " TUI_MD_ITALIC ", " TUI_MD_CODE ", " TUI_MD_HEAD ", "
.BR TUI_MD_SUM ,
each closed by one
.BR TUI_MD_OFF )
for a screen that draws the styles itself;
.BR tui_md_strip_marks ()
turns such text into plain text.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR tui_mdview_set_text (),
.BR tui_md_render (),
.BR tui_md_render_marked ()
and
.BR tui_md_strip_marks ()
return 0, or \-1 with
.I errno
.RB ( EINVAL ,
.BR ENOMEM ;
the old text stays).
.BR tui_mdview_handle ()
returns 1 when the key was a scrolling key, else 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_textview_init (3),
.BR tui_canvas_of (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
